{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>For he feared to dwell in Zoar.</b> Rashi wrote (Rashi on Genesis 19:30) because it is near Sodom. But this is not so; rather, it is because it is one of the places upon which the destruction was decreed, and by Lot's supplication the angel left it standing only because he could not flee to the mountain that day. He reasoned in his heart that it would not endure for him long, since he already had ample time to flee to the mountain. And therefore his daughter said, \"and there is no man on earth,\" for she thought that when her father left there, Zoar was destroyed."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:23.633630664Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}